Stay Safe Online – Checklist for Students

General Safety Tips
Do not click on suspicious links in emails or messages

Always verify the sender’s email address or phone number

Use strong, unique passwords for different accounts

Enable two-factor authentication (2FA) wherever possible

Avoid using public Wi-Fi for sensitive transactions

Keep your apps and devices updated regularly

Do not share personal information on unknown websites

Be cautious of messages creating urgency or fear


UPI / Financial Safety

Never share your OTP, UPI PIN, or banking details with anyone

Double-check UPI IDs and payment details before sending money

Do not accept unknown “collect requests” on UPI apps

Use only official banking and payment apps


Reporting Cybercrime (India)

National Cyber Crime Portal: https://cybercrime.gov.in

Helpline Number: 1930
